# Where `kdos app update` looks, one directory per line.
#
# A source is a directory with a `PACKAGES` index in it — a second stick, a
# mounted share, a directory somebody rsync'd a repository into. The medium
# kdos-packd reports is always consulted and needs no line here.
#
# A URL IS NEVER WRITTEN HERE, and there is no line you can uncomment to make
# this machine reach the network. That is `kdos app update --online <url>`, an
# argument, given each time: it is visible at the moment it is used, where a
# setting is invisible until the day it surprises somebody. Nothing KDOS does
# on its own leaves the machine.
#
# The index is what says which packs exist and what their payload hashes are.
# Nothing here is trusted: kdos-packd hashes and verifies every pack where the
# mount happens, so a source can offer a file and still not get it installed.
#
# /mnt/usb/packs
